SUMMARY:Sunday Sounds | Diego Vázquez
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an afternoon of music and art in the Museum. With a soundscape of piano music\, we invite you to experience artwork in the galleries in a more emotional and sensory way. \nABOUT THE MUSICIAN\nDiego Vázquez is a Spanish pianist from Madrid now based in Asheville who views music as a way to understand and express emotions beyond words. He began playing at age four and developed a strong classical foundation\, later expanding into pop and musical theater. After years of studying in Spain\, he now pursues music independently in the United States\, performing as a chapel pianist\, choir member\, and orchestra musician while also learning the organ. His cross-cultural journey shapes a deeply expressive style\, with music focused on connection rather than perfection. \nRESERVE TICKETS NOW
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/sunday-sounds-diego-vazquez-4/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Wellness
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/39d77d6f-d4f4-4e6f-ac29-15ecc83e00bc.jpg
END:VEVENT
